
@startuml
title CinemaTicket: Component Diagram (MVC, Three Layers)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Client" {
  [Browser\n(HTML, CSS, JavaScript)] as Browser
}

node "Web Server\n(Apache / XAMPP)" {

  package "Presentation Layer" {
    [public/index.php\n(Front Controller)] as Front
    [Core/View] as View
    [views/*.php\n(Templates)] as Templates
  }

  package "Business Logic Layer" {
    [Core/Router] as Router
    [Controllers\n(Auth, Film, Ticket, Admin)] as Controllers
    [Core/Auth, Session,\nValidator] as Services
  }

  package "Data Access Layer" {
    [Repositories\n(User, Film, Screening, Ticket)] as Repositories
    [Core/Database\n(PDO)] as Database
  }
}

database "MySQL / MariaDB\nCinemaTicket" as MySQL

Browser --> Front : HTTP (GET / POST)
Front --> Router : Request
Router --> Controllers : Route dispatch

Controllers --> Services : Authentication
Controllers --> Repositories : Data requests
Controllers --> View : Render page

View --> Templates : Load templates

Repositories --> Database : SQL queries
Database --> MySQL : PDO / TCP 3306

Browser ..> Front : AJAX / JSON

legend right
  MVC Architecture

  Model = Repositories + Database
  View = Core/View + views/*.php
  Controller = Controllers (through Router)

  Three Layers:
  1. Presentation Layer
  2. Business Logic Layer
  3. Data Access Layer
endlegend

@enduml
